Collect when a heap's meta data is freed into a full page.

mimalloc v3 abandons a page once it is full. A later free into that page
must claim the page and "collect" it: free it when it is empty, reclaim
it into the current theap, or re-map it so an allocator can find it
again. `_mi_free_subproc_safe` skipped that step (`allow_collect=false`)
because collecting must not cross sub-processes. Within the same
sub-process the skip is a leak: the freed block sits on the abandoned,
unmapped page's thread-free list forever, and it pins the whole page.

`mi_heap_free` frees `mi_heap_t` and `mi_arena_pages_t` through this
path, and theaps reach it through `_mi_arenas_free`. So once enough
heaps were alive at the same time to fill a page with their meta data
(9 `mi_heap_t` per 64 KiB page), every `mi_heap_destroy` leaked about
7 KiB, and about 150 KiB when the heap had allocated (its theap and its
`mi_arena_pages_t` as well). Bun creates one heap per `bun_alloc::Arena`,
for example one per `Bun.Transpiler`, and the GC destroys them in
batches, so each instance leaked that much.

This collects when the page belongs to the current sub-process.

--- a/src/free.c
+++ b/src/free.c
@@ -276,10 +276,18 @@
   mi_free_ex(p, page, NULL, false);
 }
 
-// Free a pointer that is potentially allocated in a different sub-process
+// Free a pointer that is potentially allocated in a different sub-process.
+// Collecting (free, reclaim, or re-map an abandoned page) must not cross
+// sub-processes, but it must still happen inside our own: a full page is
+// abandoned and unmapped, so a block freed into it without collecting is never
+// found again and pins the page. Heap meta data (`mi_heap_t`,
+// `mi_arena_pages_t`, theaps) is freed through here, so every destroyed heap
+// leaked it once enough heaps were alive at the same time to fill a page.
 void _mi_free_subproc_safe(void* p) mi_attr_noexcept {
-  mi_page_t* const page = mi_validate_ptr_page(p,"_mi_free_subproc_safe");  
-  mi_free_ex(p, page, NULL, false);
+  mi_page_t* const page = mi_validate_ptr_page(p,"_mi_free_subproc_safe");
+  if (page == NULL) return;
+  const bool allow_collect = (mi_page_subproc(page) == _mi_subproc());
+  mi_free_ex(p, page, NULL, allow_collect);
 }
 
 
